#* {{quote-book|be|year=1918|title=Bazylišk|author=w:Francišak Alachnovič|location=w:Vilnius|publisher=Drukarnia M. Kuchty
|page=16|pageurl=https://be.wikisource.org/wiki/Старонка:Bazylišk_(1918).pdf/18
|text=— Moj brat tak sama… Pajšoŭ, — nie wiarnuŭsia!… Jon bolš čym bratam, '''druham''' jon byŭ mnie!
|t="And also my brother… Went there,—never came back!… He was more than a brother to me—he was my '''friend'''!"}}
#* {{RQ:be:s|Домбі і сын|page=8
|— Дарагая мая Луіза, — прагаварыла міс Токс, — мой любы '''друг''', як вы сябе адчуваеце цяпер?
|origtext=en:"My dear Louisa then," said Miss Tox, "my sweet '''friend''', how are you now?"}}
#* {{RQ:be:s|Прынц і жабрак (1940)|page=109
|Што-ж ён будзе рабіць? Ва ўсім свеце ў яго ёсць адзін '''друг''' і абаронца, Майлс Гендон, і ён, натуральна, паспрабуе знайсці свайго друга, калі толькі для гэтага яму не трэба будзе вяртацца ў Лондан і рызыкаваць новымі небяспекамі.
|origtext=en:What, then, would he do? Never having had a '''friend''' in the world, or a protector, until he met Miles Hendon, he would naturally try to find that friend again, provided the effort did not require him to go toward London and danger.
|t=What, then, would he do? Having had only one '''friend''' and protector in the world, Miles Hendon, he would naturally try to find his friend, provided the effort did not require him to go toward London and risk new dangers.}}

